According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global Electric Trike Market was valued at USD 7.36 billion in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 9.995 billion by 2034, expanding at a CAGR of 4.5% during the forecast period. The market is being supported by increasing demand for compact urban mobility, expanding last-mile delivery operations, declining battery costs, and government initiatives promoting low-emission transportation.
Electric trikes are three-wheeled electric transport vehicles powered by rechargeable battery systems and electric motors. Their combination of compact dimensions, low operating costs, maneuverability, and zero tailpipe emissions makes them increasingly suitable for urban commuting, short-distance freight, community transportation, household mobility, and last-mile logistics.
